# Edges

Verify `key` and the Slack signature on the raw body before parsing. Reject a timestamp older than five minutes. Compare secrets in constant time.

A mention returns HTTP 200 with an empty body after `chat.postMessage` to that channel. `@Foosball ping` posts `pong!` and does not touch the tables. A button click returns HTTP 200 with an empty body within 3 seconds. Update the game with `chat.update` using the message timestamp from the click. An inapplicable click uses `chat.postEphemeral` and must not replace the game. `response_url` expires after 30 minutes, so it is only a fallback. `url_verification` returns the challenge. An unsigned `ssl_check=1` is accepted after the query key matches.

```typescript
// Bad: new blocks in the Lambda response to a block_actions payload
return { statusCode: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ replace_original: true, blocks }) };

// Good: ack, then update the bot's message. response_url expires after 30 minutes.
await slack.chat.update({ channel: payload.channel.id, ts: payload.message.ts, ...rendered });
return { statusCode: 200, body: "" };
```

Roster and phase writes use a condition (count still below the roster size, phase still `reporting`, user not already joined). A 1v1 write updates only the singles rating. A failed condition becomes an ephemeral reply or an idempotent re-render, never a second rating update.

Reuse `FOOSBALL_API_KEY` when deploying. DynamoDB tables are deleted with the stack. Tag stack resources `ManagedBy=foosball-aws-cdk`.
